## Writes `compiler/mir/prelude_embed.ail`: the prelude's text inside the native
## compiler, so a compiler built natively finds the `json` and `default`
## modules itself (ADR 0808):
##
##     ./ail run tools/native/gen_prelude.ail > compiler/mir/prelude_embed.ail
##
## The text is `tools/native/prelude.ail`, whole, in a raw string.

fn main() !
    text := fs.read_text("tools/native/prelude.ail")?
    print("## Generated by tools/native/gen_prelude.ail from tools/native/prelude.ail")
    print("## (json.prelude.1, ADR 0808). Do not edit; run the generator.")
    print("")
    print("pub PRELUDE_EMBED := r\"\"\"")
    print(text.trim_end())
    print("\"\"\"")
